[agent:result]     Persist the metadata and materialize the feature group to the feature store or insert data from a dataframe into the existing feature group.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     Incrementally insert data to a feature group or overwrite all data contained in the feature group.
[agent:result]     By default, the data is inserted into the offline storage as well as the online storage if the feature group is `online_enabled=True`.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     The `features` dataframe can be a Spark DataFrame or RDD, a Pandas DataFrame, a Polars DataFrame or a two-dimensional Numpy array or a two-dimensional Python nested list.
[agent:result]     If statistics are enabled, statistics are recomputed for the entire feature group.
[agent:result]     If feature group's time travel format is `HUDI` then `operation` argument can be either `insert` or `upsert`.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     If feature group doesn't exist the insert method will create the necessary metadata the first time it is invoked and writes the specified `features` dataframe as feature group to the online/offline feature store.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     Warning: Changed in 3.3.0
[agent:result]         `insert` and `save` methods are now async by default in non-spark clients.
[agent:result]         To achieve the old behaviour, set `wait` argument to `True`.
